"Autopilot: folders that keep themselves in order. Point Helm at a folder and give it rules — a file that arrives is checked against them in order, and the first one that matches is the one that runs. Sort by kind or by month, move, rename, tag, or bin; conditions include the site a file was downloaded from. A new rule is shown before it is switched on: the editor lists what is in the folder now and what would happen to each file. Nothing is ever overwritten, and nothing is acted on twice." = "“オートパイロット”: 自分で整った状態を保つフォルダ。フォルダを指定してルールを与えると、届いたファイルが上から順に照合され、最初に一致したものが実行されます。種類別・月別の整理、移動、名前変更、タグ付け、ゴミ箱へ。新しいルールは有効にする前に、いま何がどうなるかを一覧で示します。";
